 | L26 | **The page's own process (P2-2w step b; Security L5, L6, L9).** `agentos-localui` runs as its own user and reaches the owner channel only through `localui.sock` (`localui.Socket`). It keeps no session table: the phone's cookie is the token agentosd minted, and every signed-in page asks agentosd whether it is still live (`page_session`). It is given no setup hooks, no store and no Wi-Fi password (`APConfig.ValidateServe` checks only what serving needs), so every `/setup` route answers a fixed not-ready page and nothing pairs or enrolls in this process until setup moves into agentosd (P2-2w c); a box agentosd does not answer for gets the same page. It listens on the access point's address and interface only (`Listen`), and net/http's error log is discarded, so no request or form field is logged. Its unit (`cmd/agentos-localui/agentos-localui.service`) has `CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE` and `CAP_NET_RAW` (port 80, `SO_BINDTODEVICE`) and nothing else, no environment file, `MemoryMax=512M` with the Go heap's soft limit under it (L18), and IP traffic only with `10.42.0.0/24`, the default access point subnet: a box configured with another subnet changes the unit with `-addr`. Tests run the page through agentosd's real checks (`InProcess` over `localsrv`). | ARC-2, CH-7, CH-9, L15 | `cmd/agentos-localui`. |
 | L27 | **The owner line on the home page (P2-2w d2a; UX U-B1, UX-170-1; Security D1).** The signed-in home page shows the modem link's note, its last outage that ended (times in the box's zone, "Jan 2 15:04", with what did not reach the owner in the recovery text's words, or "Nothing was missed.") and the bridge's counts since agentosd started (`Others`, `TimedOut`, `Dropped`), one fixed sentence each, under "Texts with you". They come over the tokened `page_line`; the untokened `page_status` keeps the fixed note alone and no count, time or outage (D1). A fine line with no outage yet shows nothing. Not shown: an outage still open (the note says the line is down; what it misses is texted on recovery), and `Stray` (results for unknown IDs, a bridge fault rather than the owner's texts). The note's "on my Wi-Fi page" stays as is until the page has the control it names (P2-2w d2b). The page formats times in agentos-localui's `time.Local` and the recovery text in agentosd's zone; they agree because neither unit sets TZ and both read `/etc/localtime`. | CH-7, CH-1 | If counts must show before sign-in, that is a change to D1, not to this page; an open outage's running count would be a new `modemlink` accessor. |
 | L28 | **Setup's pairing and finish in agentosd (P2-2w c2; Security L6; egress K17).** On a box with no setup record finished and no owner-state file, agentosd serves only setup's four ops on `localui.sock` (`localsrv.Setup`: progress, enroll, confirm, finish) before `daemon.Run`, in the same process, and stops once finish is recorded in `-setup-record` (0600, replaced atomically); from then on, and on any restart, every setup op answers `setup closed`, and a record that cannot be read keeps setup closed. An owner-state file with no record is a hard failure, so deleting the record cannot reopen setup on an owned box. The code generator's seed is made in the vault process: the page asks for a new link each time it shows the step (each makes a new seed, at most 6 a minute), keeps only a "shown" flag so a typo needs no new scan, and holds no seed; only the newest link confirms. Only a code confirmed from the newest seed counts as enrolled, and finish has the vault seal it (L3 on #367): a new seed, as after a restart with the card's secret, voids an earlier confirmation, so a phone that lost setup does not keep the code generator. A vault whose enrollment is closed (sealed, or never opened) does not count: finish is refused, and the page's "already set up" wording for that case is the release row P2-2w c2 r1. **Carry:** before finish the page still chooses the owner number and sees each seed it renders, as it did in-process; agentosd checks only that a code was confirmed and the number is well formed. Finish's answer can race the socket closing; the page then asks `AlreadySetUp`, which says set up when agentosd does not answer setup. Progress is a fixed "ready" until the box's real progress is wired. `localui.AgentosdSetup` serves pairing, the code step and finish; networks, the box number, host trust, texts and providers are not served yet, and `cmd/agentos-localui` is still given no hooks (L26: it would need the Wi-Fi password), so a deployed box cannot pair through